> p = INLA:::inla.pc.bym.phi(graph=g, alpha = 0.5)
> phi = seq(0.0001, 0.9999, by=0.0001)
> sum(exp(p(phi)) * 0.0001)
[1] 0.9985759748

so, 'p', is a function of 0<phi<1, the mixing parameter, returning the
log prior.

doing

plot(result, plot.prior=TRUE)

will plot that prior as well,

you can also 'dig it out' from this, like if bym2 is 'region.struct',
then its there as a 'table' in the internal scale.

