By using a recent testing version it’s already there, you just have to provide a license.

You do not need to do any changes to LD_LIBRARY_PATH

Make sure it’s a newline after the license key in the file

If you’re using Ubuntu 1604 you may install another binary with

INLA:::inla.binary.install()

And chose the CentOS7 option

Let me know
